  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN272.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">iravukkuṟikkaṇ talaimakaṉ ciṟaippuṟamākat talaimakaṭkuc colluvāḷāyt tōḻi colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What the confidante said as one speaking to HER while HE was behind the hedge during the night tryst.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN272.1">
        <l>irumpuli tolaitta peruṅkai vēḻattup</l>
        <l>pula<supplied>vu</supplied>nāṟu pukarnutal kaḻumak kaṅku</l>
        <l>laruvi tanta vaṇaṅkuṭai neṭuṅkōṭ</l>
        <l>ṭañcuvaru viṭarmukai yāriru ḷakaṟṟip</l>
        <l><supplied>mi</supplied>ṉṉoḷi reḵ<supplied>ka</supplied>ñ ceṉṉeṟi viḷakkat</l>
        <l><supplied>ta</supplied>ṉiyaṉ vantu paṉi<supplied>ya</supplied>lai muṉiyā</l>
        <l>ṉīraḻi maruṅki ṉā<supplied>riṭa</supplied>t tamaṉṟa</l>
        <l>kuḷaviyoṭu miṭainta kūtaḷaṅ kaṇṇi</l>
        <l>yacaiyā nāṟṟa macaivaḷi pakarat</l>
        <l>tuṟuka ṉaṇṇiya kaṟiyivar paṭappaik</l>
        <l>kuṟiyiṟaik kurampainam maṉaivayiṟ pukutaru</l>
        <l>meymmali yuvakaiya ṉannilai kaṇṭu</l>
        <l>murukeṉa vuṇarntu mukamaṉ kūṟi</l>
        <l>yuruvac centiṉai nīroṭu tūuy</l>
        <l>neṭuvēṭ <supplied>pa</supplied>ravu maṉṉai yaṉṉō</l>
        <l>veṉṉā vatuko ṟāṉē poṉṉeṉa</l>
        <l>malarnta vēṅkai yalaṅkuciṉai yoliya</l>
        <l>maṇiniṟa maññai yakavum</l>
        <l>paṇimalai nāṭaṉō ṭamaintaṉa toṭarpē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="2">At night, when flesh-stench is copious on the dotted forehead</l>
        <l corresp="1">of the big-trunked elephant bull that destroyed the dark tiger,</l>
        <l corresp="4">dispelling the difficult darkness of fearful clefts [and] caves</l>
        <l corresp="3">in the haunted tall peaks that bring the waterfalls,</l>
        <l corresp="5">while the way to go is illuminated by [his] flashing resplendent lance</l>
        <l corresp="6">coming alone, he who does not hate the chill’s oppression,</l>
        <l corresp="12a-c">he who truly rejoices,</l>
        <l corresp="11">as he enters in our house, a short-eaved hut</l>
        <l corresp="10">in a garden where peppers climb, situated in the thick stones,</l>
        <l corresp="9">while the moving wind announces the inexhaustible scent</l>
        <l corresp="8">of [his] morning glory chaplet set close with wild jasmine,</l>
        <l corresp="7">that had grown thickly in a difficult place, by a side devoid of water,</l>
        <l rend="indent4" corresp="12d">seeing that state [of him]</l>
        <l corresp="15c">mother,</l>
        <l corresp="13">understanding it is Murukaṉ, speaks [only] praise,</l>
        <l corresp="14">sprinkles shapely red millet along with water</l>
        <l rend="indent2" corresp="15ab+d">[and] lauds great Vēḷ, alas.</l>
        <l corresp="16a-c">What will become of it?</l>
        <l corresp="19ab+d">[Our] links with the man from a land of humble mountains,</l>
        <l corresp="18">where sapphire-coloured peacocks call,</l>
        <l corresp="16d-17">while swaying branches sprout on the kino tree that blooms like gold</l>
        <l rend="indent8" corresp="19c">have become tight.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
